# Runtime handoff artifacts (regenerated each session)
.claude/handoff.md
# Listed but force-added by write-stage.sh: both halves of the task frame ARE
# tracked, as a versioned trail paired with gitlore memory commits. The listing
# keeps them out of an incidental `git add .` — only the hook adds them.
.claude/handoff-task.md
.claude/handoff-todo.md

# The armed transition and its siblings (.pending, .failed). One file, because
# at most one transition can be in flight; each exists for part of one turn (or
# one Stop -> transition window) and is consumed by a hook.
.claude/autodrive*

# handoff-checkpoint's IPC to bash-post.sh: exists for one Bash-call turn,
# consumed and deleted by the PostToolUse(Bash) hook.
.claude/checkpoint-manifest

# The checkpoint's IPC to gitlore, written on the memory directive's
# instruction and consumed by gitlore's own hooks. Listed because a `git add
# -A` in the same turn races the consumer and commits a spent trigger.
# `.claude/gitlore-hook-setup` is deliberately NOT here — that one is gitlore's
# tracked install state, not IPC.
.claude/gitlore-memory-message
.claude/gitlore-commit-memory

# Local-only Claude Code settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# uv-managed venv (created by `uv sync`; uv.lock IS tracked)
.venv/
.pytest_cache/

# macOS Finder metadata and AppleDouble sidecars. Several had accumulated
# under docs/ and got carried along by directory moves.
.DS_Store
._*
